    ":question/id": "723b13df-bde4-592d-ade7-17cdd1dad568",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-236896",
    ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed cosine function with a minimum value of $-5$ and a maximum value of $9.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{-5+9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=2.$"
  },
